Why does `this` come out undefined? (JavaScript)

```javascript
"use strict";
const counter = {
  n: 0,
  inc() { this.n++; return this.n; },
};
const f = counter.inc;
console.log(f());
```
Result:
```
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'n')
```

Copying the method into `f` detaches it from `counter`, so when it is called as a plain function `this` is `undefined` in strict mode. Call it as `counter.inc()` or bind it: `counter.inc.bind(counter)`.

Corrected version:

```javascript
const counter = {
  n: 0,
  inc() { this.n++; return this.n; },
};
const f = counter.inc.bind(counter);
console.log(f());
```

This prints:

```
1
